  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.12068v1</id>
    <title>MIRIX-2.0: Multi-Agent Memory System</title>
    <updated>2026-11-09T08:43:21Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.12068v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.12068v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Long-term memory lets LLM agents personalize, stay consistent, and reuse what worked before. Parametric memories need training, consolidation can lose details for good, and keeping every record leaves a growing store to search. We present MIRIX-2.0, a multi-agent memory system designed to be practical, accurate, and efficient at once. It is the most accurate of the compared systems on four of five QA benchmarks. It reaches 91.4% on LoCoMo and 72.6% on LongMemEval-S, where it leads the strongest baseline by 14.3 points, and with AutoDream disabled it gains 31.0 and 22.0 points over HyperMem on single-hop and multi-hop document QA. As procedural memory, it yields the highest mean success among the compared memory methods on ALFWorld and WebShop and reaches 49.2% on MetaClaw-Bench, against 44.0% for MetaClaw's skill library. Six typed memory agents keep complete records as the system of record, and a provenance hypergraph indexes episodic and semantic records with n-ary frames that cite their rows. Retrieval runs under explicit budgets, so the evidence a question inspects does not grow with the history. AutoDream merges duplicate anchors outside the write path without rewriting any record, and it distills task sessions into skills. With AutoDream disabled, MIRIX-2.0 answers faster than HyperMem on all five timed benchmarks. It needs no fine-tuning, runs with closed and open models, and its code is public.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-09T08:43:21Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Code available at https://github.com/Mirix-AI/MIRIX</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CL"/>
    <author>
      <name>Wei-Chieh Huang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Weizhi Zhang</name>
    </author>
